            <div xml:id="d197">

                <pb facs="0171" n="167" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg167"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94112/201: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Josselyn</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-08T10:00:00+08:00">August 8, 1938—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 12:07 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>With reference to my telegram August 3, 11 a.m., T. T. Quo informed me this
                    morning that he had received a telegram from the Foreign Office stating that on
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">from</hi>] August 6th the Yangtze has been
                    blockaded between Shihweiyao and Hwangchow (according to the geographic [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Geological Survey</hi>] Atlas, opposite Ocheng).</p>
                <p>Station ship informed. Sent to Ambassador.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Josselyn</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
